==============================================================================================================
PART 2. d_GW / d_EM on the C-H/K chassis: the tensor action on FRW (sympy)
==============================================================================================================
    K = 0 + 3H;   K_ij K^ij - 3H^2 = Derivative(h(t, z), t)**2/2;   a.a = 0 (khronon acceleration vanishes on this background)
    linear tensor equation:  h_tt + [3*Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t)] h_t - [1/(beta + 1)] h_zz / a^2 + [0] h = 0   (remainder 0)
    alpha_M = (friction - 3H)/H = 0;  c_T^2 = 1/(beta + 1);  mass term = 0
  [PASS] T1 friction is exactly 3H (alpha_M = 0) for symbolic (beta, c_2, alpha): no running tensor Planck mass, so Xi(z) = d_GW/d_EM = 1 exactly
           (alpha_M = 0)
  [PASS] T2 no tensor mass term on FRW (h-coefficient zero; residual zero)
           (mass = 0, residual = 0)
  [FAIL] T3 c_T^2 = 1/(1 - beta) symbolically
           (c_T^2 = 1/(beta + 1))
  [PASS] T4 the chassis used (beta = 0) is consistent with GW170817/GRB170817A: -3e-15 < c_T - 1 < 7e-16 (Abbott et al. 2017, recalled)
           (c_T - 1 = 0.000e+00)
  [PASS] K3 controls: GR gives h_tt + 3H h_t - h_zz/a^2 = 0; a time-dependent M_T^2(t) gives friction 3H + dln M_T^2/dt (= H(3 + alpha_M)), so the engine sees a running Planck mass when one exists
           (GR ok True; running-mass friction = 3*Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t) + Derivative(M2(t), t)/M2(t))
    Xi(z) on [0, 5]: min 1.000000, max 1.000000
    MOND-sector bound inside a halo (g <= 1e-9 m/s^2, L = 100 kpc, coefficient <= 1): LVK 100 Hz: dphi <= 9.1e-26 rad; LISA 1 mHz: dphi <= 9.1e-21 rad; PTA 10 nHz: dphi <= 9.1e-16 rad
  [PASS] T5 the filtered MOND sector changes GW phase by < 1e-6 rad through a 100 kpc halo at LVK, LISA and PTA frequencies
           (max 9.1e-16 rad)
    Shapiro: in candidate B the phantom is filled by cold energy (real mass on the one metric), so photons and GWs share it: dt_GW-EM = 0.
    counterfactual dark-matter emulator (GWs blind to the MW phantom; v_f 150 km/s, edge 300 kpc): dt = 157 days vs observed 1.7 s (Boran et al. 2018 class)

